F1 SVG origin probe, Chrome/156.0.8078.48, isolated ephemeral headless profile.
Reference SVG codex from committed lab/web/components.js; original SVG text is identical to reference5561530. One16pt SVG; requested device-origin phases recorded by CDP boundingClientRect.
Measured rule at1x/2x: floor(CSS origin+0.5) BEFORE device scaling. Cache contains no fractional phase. Full-size target rasters then sample1:1 on the physical grid for the measured integer DPRs.
Positive translations:1x phases0,.25,.5,.75,1,1.25,1.5,1.75 ->0,0,1,1,1,1,2,2px;2x ->0,0,0,0,2,2,2,2px. Every sprite is byte-identical to its phase0 reference after that translation.
Negative translations:1x device phases-1.5,-1,-.75,-.5,-.25,0 ->-1,-1,-1,0,0,0px;2x ->-2,0,0,0,0,0px. Each is also an exact sprite match. Native GPU regression covers signed half ties.
Competing native candidates are independent target-size resvg bitmaps: nearest-device snap, CSS snap, and shifted-SVG-viewBox baked coverage; bitmap quads avoid the production SVG placement rule.
CSS snap has lower absolute RGB error than baked coverage at all6 fractional samples; at2x .5/.75 the CSS snap also beats nearest-device snap. Phase0 error remains because resvg/tiny-skia and Chrome/Skia raster coverage differ.
Initial failed hypothesis: phase0 raster placed fractionally left56/56 reviews, mean0.648760%; baked fractional phase left56, mean0.466749%. Measured CSS snap gives48, mean0.353120% (baseline56,mean0.524382%). Threshold8,0.1% icon budget unchanged.
The initial assertion that baked phase won every sample exited1; it was disproved and replaced by the sprite translation proof. A short build failed101 while removing a stale phase variable; corrected before final build/tests. Intermediate replay workers were explicitly terminated with SIGTERM (-15); wrappers exit1. Their partial outputs/statuses are experiments, never full acceptance.
Image-read: 49-icon size grids at1x and2x plus phase triplets; web/native/diff and snapped/baked comparisons show retained silhouettes and edge coverage residue. No browser/user profile state used.
Unmeasured: fractional DPR, CSS transforms, nonintegral SVG extents, other browser/platform rasterizers. No claim for those. No filter/tap/shape/tolerance/golden changes.

